  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project for Enhancing Border Management Capacity for Responding to Infectious Diseases in Southwest Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project activities will support improved safety, security, and process efficiency at Sri Lanka and Maldives primary points of entry for international arrivals. The project sites in Sri Lanka will be the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA) at Katunayake and the Colombo Port, and in the Maldives, the project sites will be Velana International Airport and Gan International Airport. These are the currently operational airports for entry of international passengers in Sri Lanka and the Maldives. The project objective is to strengthen border measures to prevent the spread of infectious disease in preparation for revitalization of human mobility.</narrative>
  </description>
